  "body": "Behind the façade of the 1898 Gospel Hall is one of Devonport’s most substantial modern family homes. Set on a 501 sqm corner site on Calliope Road, the home spans approximately 425 sqm across three levels.\r\n\r\nStep through the entrance with its original stained glass window and kauri panelling, then follow the kauri floors past two front bedrooms and into the double-height stairwell. The staircase wraps around an ornate organ made in Chicago in 1903 and passed down from owner to owner.\r\n\r\nPast the stairs, the home opens into the kitchen and living areas. The kitchen has Italian ceramic tiles, near-new appliances and a separate scullery. In the living area, close the sliding cavity doors for a quiet evening by the gas fire, or open them up to create one large space for entertaining. Doors lead out to the north-facing deck, where lunch can turn into the whole afternoon.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the main suite has a walk-in wardrobe, an ensuite with a clawfoot bath and arched doors that open onto its own deck. From here, you can see across the rooftops to Ngataringa Bay and Takapuna, with Mount Victoria alongside and the Sky Tower to the left. Two more bedrooms and a family bathroom complete this level.\r\n\r\nAt garden level, there’s a bedroom, bathroom, living area and laundry, with a separate entrance so teenagers or visiting family can come and go on their own. Doors open onto a private garden with stone paving, a lawn and a lemon tree. There’s also space wired for a spa or sauna, a double garage with internal access and a security system.\r\n\r\nWalk five minutes to the cafés and shops on Victoria Road, the waterfront and the ferry wharf. From there, it’s a ten-minute ferry ride into the city. The beaches and golf course are also within walking distance.\r\n\r\nSEALS THE DEAL\r\n\r\nIrreplaceable scale, space for everyone to feel at home, and Devonport village just a five-minute walk from your front gate.\r\n\r\nDeadline Closing Thursday 17th of December 2026 at 2pm (unless sold prior). \r\n\r\nViewing by appointment. \r\n\r\nDisclaimer - The website may have filtered the property into a price bracket for website functionality purposes. All prospective purchasers shall complete their own due diligence, seek legal and expert advice, and satisfy themselves with respect to information supplied during the marketing of this property, including but not limited to: the floor and land sizes, boundary lines, underground services, along with any scheme plans or consents.",
